{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ופסל", :translit "ufesel", :gloss "and a carved image"} {:he "הפ\"א עקומה", :translit "ha-pe 'akumah", :gloss "the alef is bent/crooked"} {:he "לו' לך", :translit "lo, lekh", :gloss "to him: go!"} {:he "שכל המודה בע\"א כאילו כופר בכל התורה כולה", :translit "shekhol ha-modeh ba-'a'v ke'ilu kofeir bkhol ha-torah kulah", :gloss "for whoever denies idolatry is as though he affirms the entire Torah"} {:he "שניתנה מנשיקות פיהו של הקב\"ה", :translit "shenitnah mineshikot piv shel ha-kadosh barukh hu", :gloss "which was given from the kisses of His mouth of the Holy One Blessed be He"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: the letter alef in the word ופסל is written bent/crooked in the sefer Torah, read as the word לך ('go!'), urging the reader to distance from idolatry"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that one who rejects idolatry is equivalent to one who affirms the entire Torah appears in rabbinic literature (Nedarim 25a, Horayot 10a, Kiddushin 40a). The image of the Torah being given from the kisses of His mouth derives from Song of Songs 1:2, 'for your love is better than wine,' which midrashic tradition reads as referring to the words of Torah flowing from the divine mouth (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:9).", :sources ["Nedarim 25a" "Horayot 10a" "Kiddushin 40a" "Song of Songs 1:2" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: the letter alef in the word ופסל is written bent/crooked in the sefer Torah, read as the word לך ('go!'), urging the reader to distance from idolatry", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:55.884017553Z", :model "glm-5.2"}